  {
    "id": "a0c714d7de4775dd8e95f08d",
    "path": "datafusion_functions_aggregate_common::order::AggregateOrderSensitivity::SoftRequirement",
    "name": "SoftRequirement",
    "owner": "datafusion_functions_aggregate_common::order::AggregateOrderSensitivity",
    "crate": "datafusion-functions-aggregate-common",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "variant",
    "signature": "SoftRequirement",
    "docs": "Indicates that the aggregator is more efficient when the input is ordered\nbut can still produce its result correctly regardless of the input ordering.\nThis is similar to, but stronger than, [`Self::Beneficial`].\n\nSimilarly to [`Self::HardRequirement`], when possible DataFusion will insert\na `SortExec`, to reorder the input to match the SoftRequirement. However,\nwhen such a `SortExec` cannot be inserted, (for example, due to conflicting\n[`Self::HardRequirement`] with other ordered aggregates in the query),\nthe aggregate function will still execute, without the preferred order, unlike\nwith [`Self::HardRequirement`]",
